"Kent Paul Dolan" <xanthian@well.com> writes:
> As each conduct is broken, it would be nice if the
> game messaged the player "so much for conduct %s
> [you clumsy oaf(*)]";
>
> This doesn't seem particularly hard to implement

Not hard, but a pain; the way conducts work at present is by
incrementing a counter for _every_ action that could break a conduct,
and #conduct just checks to see which counters are still at zero. To
give a message, you'd either need to add a check at each increment to
see whether it's being incremented from zero, or add a global check at
the moveloop stage to see if any counters went non-zero that turn;
either would be an awkward thing to have to do.

